<title>UK: Mid Kent falls after takeover bid blocked.</title>
<headline>Mid Kent falls after takeover bid blocked.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in water company Mid Kent Holdings fell on Tuesday after Britain's Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) said it had prohibited a proposed takeover bid for the company.</p>
<p>The stock was trading at 575p, down 60p at 1200 GMT.</p>
<p>The hostile bid was proposed by General Utilities Plc and SAUR Water Services Plc, both local units of larger French groups. But the DTI decided the merger would be against the public interest.</p>
<p>This is the first time the stock has fallen below 600p since November 22 last year.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
